  "title": "US Intelligence Chief Jay Clayton Defends Trump's 'My Friend' Remarks",
  "summary": "Jay Clayton, the US director of national intelligence, defended President Donald Trump's characterization of Russian leader Vladimir Putin as'my friend' during a rare three-way summit in China. He emphasized that the remarks were entirely appropriate in context, highlighting the importance of the summit despite concerns about its substance.",
  "facts": [
    {
      "statement": "Jay Clayton, the US director of national intelligence, said President Donald Trump's remarks were 'entirely appropriate' in context.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "Jay Clayton defended the remarks as part of a rare three-way summit with Putin and China's President Xi Jinping.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "The summit, despite its symbolism, was described as a historic gathering of the three countries.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    }
