  "sources": [
    {
      "title": "US intelligence chief says he trusts Trump’s description of Putin as ‘my friend’",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/nov/22/intelligence-chief-jay-clayton-trump-putin-my-friend",
      "description": "<p>Jay Clayton was pressed on Trump’s characterization of Putin during media appearances on Sunday</p><p>Jay Clayton, the US director of national intelligence, said he trusts Donald Trump “completely” after the US president called Vladimir Putin “a friend” during <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/video/2026/nov/19/trump-greets-putin-before-holding-talks-at-apec-summit-video\">their recent meeting</a> in China.</p><p>Clayton made the remarks on Sunday, where he was pressed during media appearances on Trump’s warm characterization of the Russian president – who is viewed as a chief US adversary – following his trilateral summit with Putin and China’s Xi Jinping. After a backlash at home and aboard, Trump doubled down on Saturday and <a href=\"https://truthsocial.com/@realDonaldTrump/posts/117656427563362319\">posted a photo of himself and Putin </a>shaking hands with the caption “My Friend.”</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/nov/22/intelligence-chief-jay-clayton-trump-putin-my-friend\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-11-22T20:55:33"
    },
    {
      "title": "US intelligence chief defends Trump’s comments calling Putin his ‘friend’",
      "link": "https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/11/23/us-intelligence-chief-defends-trumps-comments-calling-putin-his?traffic_source=rss",
      "description": "US Director of National Intelligence Jay Clayton says Trump&#039;s comments were &#039;entirely appropriate&#039; in context of summit.",
      "source_name": "Al Jazeera All News",
      "published": "2026-11-23T02:23:13"
    },
    {
      "title": "Trump's description of Putin as a friend is entirely appropriate: DNI chief",
      "link": "https://www.business-standard.com/world-news/trump-s-description-of-putin-as-a-friend-is-entirely-appropriate-dni-chief-126112200856_1.html",
      "description": "Director of National Intelligence Jay Clayton said Sunday it was \"entirely appropriate\" for President Donald Trump to call Russian leader Vladimir Putin his friend.\nClayton defended comments that Democrats have characterized as a betrayal of American values after Trump met with Putin and Chinese President Xi Jinping for rare three-way talks. The summit last week in China seemed to be more symbolism than substance, but Trump and his top aides have described it as a historic gathering of the three countries with the largest nuclear arsenals.\nTrump raised eyebrows with his warm greeting of Putin and repeated references to him as his \"friend,\" which continued on Saturday, when the Republican president posted an image on Truth Social of him shaking hands with a smiling Putin under the caption, \"My Friend.\"\n\"In that circle - in that circle of that conversation, using the term friend' is entirely appropriate,\" Clayton said on ABC's \"This Week.\"\nHe had a similar assessment on CNN's \"State",
      "source_name": "Business Standard Latest",
      "published": "2026-11-23T02:15:31"
    }
